.TH mdns-tui-browser 1 "2026-11-14" "mdns-tui-browser" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
mdns-tui-browser \- terminal-based mDNS service browser

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdns-tui-browser
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
A terminal-based mDNS service browser built with Rust. It provides an interactive TUI interface for discovering and browsing mDNS services on the local network, with real-time updates, service filtering, and sorting capabilities. Services advertised by the local device are highlighted with a marker, addresses show interface information, and service URLs can be opened in the browser.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-service-types \fISERVICE_TYPES\fR
Service types to browse for (e.g., http, _http._tcp, printer)
Auto-completes (_)service, (_)sub, .(_)[tc|ud]p and .local. suffix
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interfaces \fIINTERFACES\fR
Network interfaces to use for mDNS discovery (e.g., en0, eth0)
Can be specified multiple times or comma-separated
.TP
.B \-\-no-ipv4
Disable IPv4 mDNS discovery
.TP
.B \-\-no-ipv6
Disable IPv6 mDNS discovery
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-load-state \fIFILE\fR
Load state from a JSON file for inspection (view-only mode, no browsing)

.SH SERVICE TYPES
The \fB\-\-service-types\fR argument supports various formats:
.RS
.IP \(bu
Simple names: \fBhttp\fR, \fBssh\fR, \fBprinter\fR
.IP \(bu
Partial forms: \fB_http\fR, \fB_http._tcp\fR
.IP \(bu
Protocol spec: \fBhttp.tcp\fR, \fBssh.tcp\fR
.IP \(bu
Subtypes: \fBprinter.sub.http\fR
.IP \(bu
Full forms: \fB_http._tcp.local.\fR
.RE

.PP
Common service types:
.RS
.IP \(bu
\fBhttp\fR - HTTP servers
.IP \(bu
\fBssh\fR - SSH servers
.IP \(bu
\fBprinter\fR - Network printers
.IP \(bu
\fBairplay\fR - Apple AirPlay devices
.IP \(bu
\fBraop\fR - AirPlay audio devices
.RE

.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B Navigation
.br
↑/↓ or j/k             - Navigate services list
.br
←/→ or h/l             - Switch between service types
.br
H/L                    - Page through service types
.br
Ctrl+Home/End          - Jump to first/last service type
.br
PageUp/PageDown or b/f or Space - Scroll services list by page
.br
Home/End               - Jump to first/last service
.br
Enter                 - Open service URL in browser (shows selection popup when multiple URLs exist)
.br
Shift+↑/↓ or J/K       - Scroll service details
.TP
.B Sorting
.br
s                      - Cycle sort field forward (Host → Type → Name → Port → Addr → Time)
.br
S                      - Cycle sort field backward (Time → Addr → Port → Name → Type → Host)
.br
o                      - Toggle sort direction (↑/↓)
.TP
.B Filtering
.br
/                      - Enter quick filter mode (search across all service fields)
.br
n                      - Clear current filter
.br
d                      - Remove offline services
.br
D                      - Clear stale service types (service types with no services)
.TP
.B Other
.br
m                      - Show service metrics
.br
Ctrl+J                 - Dump current state to JSON file
.br
Ctrl+Z                 - Suspend the application (Unix only)
.br
?                      - Toggle help popup
.br
q or Ctrl+c            - Quit the application
.TP
.B URL Selection Popup
.br
↑/↓                    - Navigate URLs
.br
Enter                  - Open selected URL
.br
Esc or any other key   - Cancel and close popup
.TP
.B Help Popup Controls
.br
↑/↓                    - Scroll help content
.br
r                      - Open release notes in browser
.br
Any other key          - Close help popup
.PP
\fBNote:\fR When loading a state file with \fB\-\-load-state\fR, the application runs in view-only mode (no browsing). The border color changes to a darker color to indicate this mode.

.SH QUICK FILTER
The quickfilter feature allows searching across all service fields using typo-tolerant fuzzy matching and status keywords.
.PP
To activate quickfilter mode, press \fB/\fR. Then type your search query and press \fBEnter\fR to apply or \fBEsc\fR to cancel.
.PP
The quickfilter searches across these service fields:
.RS
.IP \(bu
Service fullname and name
.IP \(bu
Host address
.IP \(bu
Service type and subtype
.IP \(bu
IP addresses
.IP \(bu
Port number
.IP \(bu
TXT record contents
.RE
.PP
Whitespace-separated terms must all match, in any order. A term's characters must appear in order but need not be adjacent. Terms of four or more characters tolerate one typo; shorter terms tolerate none. Services where every term appears contiguously are listed first, then closer fuzzy matches; the selected sort breaks ties.
.PP
The reserved words \fBonline\fR, \fBoffline\fR, and \fBflapping\fR filter by service status instead of matching text. They are case-insensitive and combine with each other and with text terms; every one must hold:
.RS
.IP \(bu
\fBonline\fR - Only online services
.IP \(bu
\fBoffline\fR - Only offline services
.IP \(bu
\fBflapping\fR - Only flapping services (at least 3 sessions with at least half shorter than 5 minutes)
.RE
.PP
Examples:
.RS
.IP \(bu
\fBprn\fR - Matches services such as "printer"
.IP \(bu
\fBonline http\fR - Show online services matching "http"
.IP \(bu
\fBonline flapping\fR - Show services that are both online AND flapping
.IP \(bu
\fBonline offline\fR - Shows nothing (contradictory status)
.RE
.PP
Quick filter mode controls:
.RS
.IP \(bu
\fBEnter\fR - Apply filter
.IP \(bu
\fBEsc\fR - Cancel filter input
.IP \(bu
\fBBackspace\fR - Delete last character
.IP \(bu
Any other key - Type search text (case-insensitive)
.RE

.SH ADD SERVICE TYPE
To add a new service type while the application is running, press \fBa\fR. Then type the service type name and press \fBEnter\fR to add and start browsing, or \fBEsc\fR to cancel.

.SH LOCAL DEVICE HIGHLIGHT
Services whose resolved address matches one of this device's network interface addresses are marked as local: a ◉ prefix plus bold green highlighting in the services list, and a ◉ Advertised by this device banner at the top of the service details. Interface addresses refresh every 30 seconds, so VPN/DHCP changes are picked up without restart. Link-local addresses (fe80::/10 IPv6, 169.254/16 IPv4) only match on the same interface.

.SH OPENING SERVICE URLS
Press \fBEnter\fR on a service to open its URL. URLs come from TXT records (any key=value with an http:// or https:// value) and, for service types containing \(lqhttp\(rq, constructed scheme://host:port/path URLs for the hostname plus every resolved IP (IPv6 bracketed, link-local IPv6 skipped; https scheme when the service type contains \(lqhttps\(rq, path from the path= TXT record). With no URLs a status message is shown; with one URL it opens directly; with multiple URLs a Select URL popup offers the choice.

.SH SERVICE ADDRESSES
The details pane shows which interface each address was seen on (live browsing): IPv4 as \(lq192.168.1.10 via eth0\(rq, IPv6 link-local as \(lqfe80::1%eth0\(rq (interface index on Windows), and IPv6 global as \(lq2001:db8::1 via eth0, wlan0\(rq. The services list shows only the first address as a bare IP. State dumps do not preserve interface information, so loaded dumps show bare addresses.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
Setting the NO_COLOR environment variable to any non-empty value (see https://no-color.org/) disables colors. The interface remains usable through text attributes: selected rows use reverse video, offline services stay struck through, and flapping services stay underlined.

.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.IP \(bu
Browse auto-discovered services:
.br
.B mdns-tui-browser
.IP \(bu
Browse explicit service types:
.br
.B mdns-tui-browser \-\-service-types "_http._tcp.local.,_ssh._tcp.local."
.IP \(bu
Browse with shortened service types:
.br
.B mdns-tui-browser \-s "http,ssh"
.IP \(bu
Browse with shortened service types, specified multiple times:
.br
.B mdns-tui-browser \-s http \-s ssh
.IP \(bu
Browse using a specific network interface:
.br
.B mdns-tui-browser \-i eth0
.IP \(bu
Browse using multiple network interfaces:
.br
.B mdns-tui-browser \-\-interfaces en0,eth0
.IP \(bu
Disable IPv4 mDNS discovery:
.br
.B mdns-tui-browser \-\-no-ipv4
.IP \(bu
Disable IPv6 mDNS discovery:
.br
.B mdns-tui-browser \-\-no-ipv6
.IP \(bu
Load state from a JSON file (view-only mode):
.br
.B mdns-tui-browser \-\-load-state state-dump.json
.RE

